{"kind":"assert","text":"Required same-commitment correction for the independent #22093 review at exact e66a29775d7050e1158398de0b7e7cbc6f9e4297: enforce the adopted before-signing size boundary when the local configuration has no ceiling. This confirms the source-level question I sent before the final packet was filed. It does not request a new outcome, change Hugh's adoption, or claim the kernel admits oversized events.\n\nThe [signing path](internal/app/app.go@e66a29775d7050e1158398de0b7e7cbc6f9e4297:1997) skips ValidateUnsignedRequestSize when config.PayloadCeiling is zero. The [new fallback test](internal/app/sign_ceiling_test.go@e66a29775d7050e1158398de0b7e7cbc6f9e4297:84) exercises only an ordinary small act. The [architecture paragraph](docs/reference/architecture.md@e66a29775d7050e1158398de0b7e7cbc6f9e4297:1827) acknowledges the missing early check, while [limits.md](docs/reference/limits.md@e66a29775d7050e1158398de0b7e7cbc6f9e4297:51) says one before-signing boundary covers every surface. The adopted proposal ddaf3197 explicitly requires refusal before signing on gs state, MCP state and resident /v0/act; preserving kernel refusal after a signature exists does not meet that condition.\n\nI independently tested a disposable git archive of this exact head under Go1.26.7. A synthetic workroom has an authoritative genesis ceiling of 2,048 bytes. I cloned its local configuration, changed only the recorded ceiling to zero to simulate the supported legacy configuration, saved it and reopened normally, preserving its custody and verified-frontier fields. Submitting 4,096 evidence bytes returns the correct kernel ceiling error, leaves the frontier unchanged, and records exactly one signature through this head's own signatureCounter. The final output reports a 4,802-byte measured act against the 2,048-byte ceiling. The existing normal-ceiling before-signing test passes alongside it with its zero-signature rejection control. Both tests passed in the diagnostic run; that means the counterexample was observed, not that the candidate meets the missing condition. The test, commands and output are attached.\n\nThis is a local application-path counterexample, not an end-to-end remote attached-client test. No live configuration, resident, witness or repository source was changed. The first probe changed only the in-memory ceiling and correctly hit the immutable-config consistency guard; the corrected fixture changes the stored synthetic configuration and reopens it, so that unrelated guard cannot explain the final result.\n\nObtain the authoritative ceiling before signing on this supported path, retaining the kernel's final enforcement and unchanged ordinary/accepted-retry behavior. Use a meaningful zero-local-ceiling oversized control and preserve no-signature/no-append assertions; do not solve it by weakening the adopted condition or broadly refusing every legacy/attached workroom. Reconcile the contract prose with the actual behavior. Correct this on promise c2c18651, publish the new exact head with this finding, and obtain fresh independent review. The smallest adequate change is preferred; no timing campaign, new locator design, deployment or separate adoption is requested.","body":{"head":"e66a29775d7050e1158398de0b7e7cbc6f9e4297","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:49846f737a726a4c9bb50db06e7e65d841d41ba7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:59154b8746afa9148f9c48026b269b6fdaabc8b1, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:789e3da135b2b0a7f8317667024479a2ed74ccaa, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8aa561dc1cceecd5fe41a286d07bb091b48669e6, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c2c186516fa6f2df92a9b2d23f605c5bf744c388 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb90201bc66c1c6a26, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:005460183c8